{{Quote|And the Jedi's opponent&hellip;from the dolovite mines of Mustafar&hellip;where for years his job was to keep the tunnels clear of xandanks and giant man-eating lava eels.|Fight announcer at the Grakkus Arena|<ref name="SW11" />}}
The '''dolovite mines of Mustafar''' contained tunnels that were guarded by the [[roggwart]] [[Kongo]] against [[xandank]]s and [[lava eel]]s. The [[Mining|mines]] were located on<ref name="SW11" /> the [[Volcano|volcanic]] mining [[planet]] [[Mustafar]]; under the heavy guard of the [[Galactic Empire]], mining operations there eventually ceased by the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Tales1">[[Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle 1|''Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle'' 1]]</ref> While Kongo enjoyed killing the giant [[eel]]s with his bare [[Limb|hands]] at the [[dolovite]] mines, he became a [[gladiator]] at the [[Grakkus Arena]] on [[Nar Shaddaa]] by [[0 ABY]]. In that [[Standard year|year]], an announcer of [[Grakkus Jahibakti Tingi|Grakkus's]] arena detailed the roggwart's work at the mines while the beast, dubbed "Kongo the Disemboweler," was released to combat the [[Jedi]]-in-[[Jedi training|training]] [[Luke Skywalker]].<ref name="SW11" />

==Behind the scenes==
The dolovite mines of Mustafar were mentioned in the [[Star Wars (2015) 11|eleventh issue]] of the [[Star Wars comic books|comic series]] [[Star Wars (2015)|''Star Wars'']],<ref name="SW11" /> written by [[Jason Aaron]] and published by [[Marvel Comics]] on [[November 4]], [[2015]].<ref name="PREVIEWSworld">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/52662/star_wars_2015_11|text=Star Wars (2015) #11}}</ref>

